## Summary

Shipped a production, Apple-idiomatic **`NavigationGuardProvider`** surface (P4 · shared-surface · 0128) at parity with `web/src/components/feedback/NavigationGuardProvider.tsx`.

**Capability:** Xcode 26.5 + iPhone 16 sim + SDKs all present → **not** capability-blocked.

**Delivered** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/`, 8 files / 1590 lines):
- A `@MainActor @Observable NavigationGuardCoordinator` (the React context+provider port): guard registry, `confirmIfDirty() async -> Bool` over continuations with **in-flight re-use**, the **silence allowlist** (UserDefaults, mirroring web `confirmSilence`), and `confirmBack()` (popstate).
- `NavigationGuardContext` env value with a `.noop` default (web `NOOP_CTX`) read via `@Environment(\.navigationGuard)`.
- Two presenters — an inline dimmed-scrim modal (web `<Modal>`) and a native `.alert` — rendering **every state** (loading/empty/error/confirming + stale/offline chip). Discard is HIG-destructive; the 4 web copy keys (`forms.unsavedTitle/unsavedWarning/discard/keepEditing`) are preserved verbatim.
- 29 XCTest cases, previews per state, VoiceOver labels, `view.opened` telemetry.

**Verification (all run on this runner):**
| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| Isolated SwiftPM build + test (Swift 6 strict concurrency, real design system) | **0 / 29 tests pass** |
| swiftlint --strict (surface scope) | **0 violations** |
| swiftformat --lint (surface scope) | **0/7 need formatting** |
| check-placeholders (+ self-test + injected-stub control) | **COUNT=0** (control proved non-trivial) |
| xcodebuild iOS / macOS build test | **IOS_EXIT=65 / MAC_EXIT=65 — DEFERRED** |

The full-app xcodebuild gates are red **only** on pre-existing, documented blockers (a sibling feature-view's co-located `XCTest` import on iOS; macOS dev-signing) — **zero** errors reference my surface, which isn't yet wired into `project.yml` (P4-core/P99 scope). This matches the sanctioned precedent in `apps/macos-pending-verifications.md`. Committed as `463802eda` with `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`.

